# 22. Most Important Product Principle

Do not build features because they are listed in this document.

Build around the customer's actual workflow.

The first real pharmacy is the design partner.

Instrument the product and observe:

* where the cashier gets stuck
* what the owner asks
* what reports they need
* what they currently do manually
* what information they cannot easily obtain
* what they repeatedly complain about

The product should evolve from real operational data.

---

# 23. Definition of Success

The first customer should be able to say:

> "I can run my chemist from this."

A cashier should be able to process a sale in seconds.

An M-Pesa customer should receive an STK prompt without the cashier leaving the POS.

The owner should be able to open the dashboard and understand the business immediately.

And eventually the owner should be able to ask:

> **"What's happening in my business?"**

and receive a useful, data-backed answer.

Build the foundation for that company—not merely another POS.
